    "title": "Lady Canes claim shut out at Basilica - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By J.W. COOKE ,\n5 hours ago\nKEY WEST — For the first time in more than 40 years, a Coral Shores High sports program took part in a contest on the St. Mary's campus, against the Basilica volleyball team on Thursday, Aug. 21.\nThe squad met last season on the Lady Canes campus on Plantation Key during the Mariners' first varsity campaign since 1986, and for a second straight year, Coral Shores last week came out with a 3-0 win, officially opening the 2025 schedule with a 25-17, 25-10, 25-21 triumph.\nCoral Shores, which swept Key West and Marathon in the preseason tournament, was to take on its first out-of-county opponent on Monday, Aug. 25, hosting Somerset SOHO, before facing Mater Bay Academy on Wednesday, Aug. 27. The Lady Canes head back south to play at Key West High School on Aug. 28 at 5:30 p.m.",
